  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The Manual states that, before registration, the Registrar may revoke acceptance if satisfied of both conditions below; revocation is discretionary, not automatic.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part38/2#1",
          "quote": "Before a trade mark is registered, the Registrar may revoke the acceptance of the application for registration of the trade mark if he or she is satisfied that:"
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "First, the Registrar must be satisfied that the application should not have been accepted, considering all circumstances existing when it was accepted—including circumstances unknown to the Registrar at that time.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part38/2#1",
          "quote": "a. the application should not have been accepted, taking account of all the circumstances that existed when the application was accepted (whether or not the Registrar knew then of their existence); and"
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "Second, the Registrar must be satisfied that revoking acceptance is reasonable, taking account of all the circumstances.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part38/2#1",
          "quote": "b. it is reasonable to revoke the acceptance, taking account of all the circumstances."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "These conditions are reported from the Manual's account of subsection 38(1); the supplied legislation does not include section 38, so its statutory wording and any further procedural requirements cannot be verified from the supplied legislative passages.",
